{"version":1,"rules":[{"id":"odin","ignorable":false,"why":"Every package must compile under odx's strict flags, since odx's rules need valid Odin.","fix":"Fix the compiler error or warning that the message quotes."},{"id":"parse-unsupported","ignorable":false,"why":"A file odx can't read or parse gets none of the rules that need its syntax tree.","fix":"Make it a regular .odin file with a package clause that core:odin/parser can parse."},{"id":"import-escape","ignorable":false,"why":"A result must depend only on the repo and the Odin root, not on code outside them.","fix":"Bring the code into the repo, or import it from the Odin root's base, core or vendor."},{"id":"path-case","ignorable":false,"why":"A miscased path works on a case-insensitive disk and breaks on a case-sensitive one.","fix":"Spell the path in the exact case of the entries on disk."},{"id":"line-length","ignorable":true,"why":"Lines stay within 100 columns, with a tab counted as 4, so code reads without wrapping.","fix":"Break the line to fit 100 columns; an ignore with a reason is the exception."},{"id":"ignore-invalid","ignorable":false,"why":"An ignore odx can't apply looks like an exception while it suppresses nothing.","fix":"Write // odx:ignore <rules> <reason> above the code, naming only ignorable rules."},{"id":"ignore-unused","ignorable":false,"why":"An ignore that suppresses nothing is a stale exception that could hide a later finding.","fix":"Delete the ignore, or move it directly above the code that has the finding."},{"id":"pending-stale","ignorable":false,"why":"Pending is debt to fix, so an entry with nothing left to fix leaves the list.","fix":"Remove the entry from pending in odx.json, or correct it to name a package odx checks."},{"id":"block-comment","ignorable":false,"why":"Line comments are the one comment form, so every comment reads the same way.","fix":"Rewrite the comment as // line comments."},{"id":"one-line-block","ignorable":false,"why":"A short body has two forms only: do on one line, or braces on lines of their own.","fix":"Write the body with do on one line, or put each brace on its own line."},{"id":"auto-cast","ignorable":false,"why":"auto_cast hides the target type, so a reader can't see what the conversion does.","fix":"Name the type, as cast(T)x or T(x)."},{"id":"fallthrough","ignorable":true,"why":"Each switch case stands alone, so no case's code runs on into the next one.","fix":"Share code via one case list or a procedure; an ignore with a reason is the exception."},{"id":"bounds-check-directive","ignorable":true,"why":"Bounds checking follows the build's flags, not a directive that changes it for one block.","fix":"Remove the directive; an ignore with a reason is the exception."},{"id":"vet-disabled","ignorable":false,"why":"Every file gets the compiler's vet checks, so a #+vet tag can't turn one off for a file.","fix":"Remove the items that turn checks off, and fix what the compiler then reports."},{"id":"feature-relaxed","ignorable":true,"why":"A #+feature tag turns off a compiler error that protects the file, such as using-stmt.","fix":"Remove the tag and fix what it hid; the exception is a whole-file ignore with a reason."},{"id":"transmute","ignorable":true,"why":"transmute reinterprets bits with no check that they make sense as the new type.","fix":"Use a cast or a conversion; an ignore with a reason is the exception."},{"id":"format","ignorable":false,"why":"All code has the formatter's layout, so a diff shows only real changes.","fix":"Run odinfmt with the odinfmt.json that odx init writes, and keep its output."},{"id":"proc-length","ignorable":true,"why":"A procedure body of over 100 counted lines is too long to read as one unit.","fix":"Split the procedure into smaller ones; an ignore with a reason is the exception."},{"id":"nesting-depth","ignorable":true,"why":"Blocks nested more than 6 deep are hard to follow.","fix":"Return early or extract a procedure; an ignore with a reason is the exception."},{"id":"name-case","ignorable":true,"why":"Each kind of name has one case, so a name shows if it is a type, procedure or constant.","fix":"Rename it in the case the message names, using @(link_name) for a foreign symbol."},{"id":"package-name","ignorable":false,"why":"A package is named for its directory, in snake_case, so an import path shows its name.","fix":"Rename the package or its directory to one snake_case name, or name the package main."},{"id":"file-name","ignorable":false,"why":"File names are snake_case like package names, so every path in the repo has one form.","fix":"Rename the file in snake_case, such as my_file.odin."},{"id":"import-alias","ignorable":false,"why":"An alias equal to the import's own name is noise that looks like a rename.","fix":"Remove the alias."},{"id":"import-order","ignorable":false,"why":"Imports keep one order, so a reader finds each one where the order puts it.","fix":"Order imports base and core, vendor, collections, relative, a blank line between groups."}]}
